From 8fa42e8f856f720b7e09909de0590c3cba4d500e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:23:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw: a write to a missing hardware file starts from the /boot
 copy

Why: when only /boot/firmware/apertar-hardware.conf exists, an IMU write
(calibrate_gyro, set_imu_sync_offset, ...) went through the config store,
which treated the missing editable file as empty text. It then created
/home/pi/apertar-hardware.conf holding only the IMU keys. Every reader
takes the first file of the candidate list, so on the next start the
buttons, displays and the rest of the /boot sections were gone. Original
Apertar writes only the editable path (App:4271-4276@upstream-1.6.0) and
its IMU wrote the file the loader read
(Mpu6050RecordingSession.cpp:1297-1300@upstream-1.6.0), so nothing was
lost.

What: HardwareConfigStore::saveLocked starts from the text of
/boot/firmware/apertar-hardware.conf, else /boot/apertar-hardware.conf,
when the editable file does not exist. That is the rule the Config page
already uses (buildHardwareConfigFileJson). The write still goes only to
the editable path.

Tested: check_core.sh both tests (PASS). --simulate in a private mount
namespace with a tmpfs /boot holding a /boot/firmware copy and
APERTAR_HARDWARE_CONFIG on a missing file: set_imu_sync_offset 12
created the editable file with every /boot section and the new value.
Pi: nothing needed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
index 872f166..995756c 100644
--- a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
@@ -273,7 +273,16 @@ StoreResult HardwareConfigStore::saveLocked(const std::string &base, const std::
         return result;
     }
 
-    const std::string current = text_;
+    // A missing file starts from a /boot copy when there is one: the readers take its sections, so a write must keep them.
+    std::string current = text_;
+    if (!stamp_.exists) {
+        for (const char *candidate : { "/boot/firmware/apertar-hardware.conf", "/boot/apertar-hardware.conf" }) {
+            if (std::filesystem::is_regular_file(candidate, error)) {
+                current = readTextFile(candidate);
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
     const std::string currentRevision = revision_;
     const hwconf::Document currentDoc = hwconf::parse(current);
     std::vector<hwconf::Edit> merged;
